# Example secret word list for the sensitive_content PreToolUse handler
# (handlers.pre_tool_use.sensitive_content, Plan 00201).
#
# Copy this file to `.claude/block-words.secret` (already gitignored via the
# `*.secret` pattern) and replace the placeholder lines below with your own
# terms. Never commit, print, or paste the real file's contents anywhere --
# that defeats the entire point of this mechanism.
#
# Format:
#   - One term per line.
#   - Lines starting with `#` are comments and are ignored.
#   - Blank lines are ignored.
#   - Matching is case-insensitive and LITERAL -- a term containing regex
#     metacharacters (e.g. `a.b*c`) is matched only as that exact substring,
#     never interpreted as a pattern.
#   - Order matters only in that it fixes each term's 1-based index, which is
#     the ONLY thing ever surfaced about a match (in a deny reason, this QA
#     script's output, or anywhere else) -- the term text itself is never
#     shown, logged, captured, or archived.
#
# Good candidates for this file: employer/client names, internal hostnames,
# real people's names, project codenames -- any specific identifier that
# would be embarrassing or sensitive to leak, but which you don't want named
# even in this tracked repo's own config (unlike `public_patterns`, which
# ARE safe to name because they describe a structural SHAPE rather than a
# specific identifier).
#
# Example placeholder terms (delete these and add your own):
example-employer-name
example-internal-hostname
example-person-name
